lic>-hydroxybenzyl)thiamin)Cl<sub>3</sub> &#x000b7; H<sub>2</sub>O</article-title><source><italic>Journal of the American Chemical Society</italic></source><year>1990</year><volume>112</volume><issue>20</issue><fpage>7233</fpage><lpage>7238</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Louloudi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadjiliadis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Lussac</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bau</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transition and group IIB metal complexes with &#x0201c;active aldehyde&#x0201d; derivatives of thiamine</article-title><source><italic>Metal-Based Drugs</italic></source><year>1994</year><volume>1</volume><issue>2-3</issue><fpage>221</fpage><lpage>231</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dodi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerothanassis</surname><given-names>IP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadjiliadis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Complexes of Zn<sup>2+</sup>, Cd<sup>2+</sup>, and Hg<sup>2+</sup> with 2-(<italic>&#x003b1;</italic>-Hydroxybenzyl)thiamine monophosphate chloride</article-title><source><italic>Inorganic Chemistry</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>35</volume><issue>22</issue><fpage>6513</fpage><lpage>6519</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11666799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malandrinos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Louloudi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitsopoulou</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>IS</given-names></name><name><surname>Bau</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadjiliadis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the mechanism of action of thiamin enzymes, crystal structure of 2- (<italic>&#x003b1;</italic>-hydroxyethyl)thiamin pyrophosphate (HETPP). Complexes of HETPP with zinc(II) and cadmium(II)</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Biological Inorganic Chemistry</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>3</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>437</fpage><lpage>448</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malandrinos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Louloudi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Koukkou</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name><name><surname>Sovago</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Drainas</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadjiliadis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Zinc(II) and cadmium(II) metal complexes of thiamine pyrophosphate and 2-(<italic>&#x003b1;</italic>-hydroxyethyl)thiamine pyrophosphate: models for activation of pyruvate decarboxylase</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Biological Inorganic Chemistry</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>5</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>226</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10819467</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malandrinos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Louloudi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Deligiannakis</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadjiliadis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two-dimensiona